---
import BenchPage from '../../layouts/BenchPage.astro';
import MethodConstellations from '../../components/coffee/MethodConstellations.svelte';
import { ATLAS, CONTACT, FILTER, FORCE, brewGuideHref, ratioText, timeText } from '../../lib/coffee/methodAtlas.ts';
import { EXPLORE_SOURCES } from '../../lib/coffee/explore-sources.ts';

const title = 'Coffee Brewing Methods Compared: Brewing Constellations';
const description = 'Thirteen coffee brewers compared on how water meets the coffee, the filter, what pushes the water and brew time. Compare any two side by side and open a recipe.';
const cited = ['easto', 'hoffmann', 'rao', 'synthesis'].map((id) => EXPLORE_SOURCES[id]);
const order = ['percolation', 'steep-drain', 'immersion'] as const;
const rows = [...ATLAS].sort((a, b) => order.indexOf(a.contact) - order.indexOf(b.contact) || a.timeS[0] - b.timeS[0]);
---

<BenchPage
  title={title}
  description={description}
  kicker="Explore · Brewing Constellations"
  lede="Thirteen brewers as stars, and four ways to arrange the sky."
  back={{ href: '/explore/', label: 'The gallery' }}
  gallery
  wide
  schema={[{
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'WebApplication',
    name: 'Brewing Constellations',
    url: 'https://jayarr.coffee/explore/methods/',
    description,
    applicationCategory: 'EducationalApplication',
    operatingSystem: 'Any',
    offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '0', priceCurrency: 'USD' },
    publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'JayArr Coffee', url: 'https://jayarr.coffee' },
  }]}
>
  <Fragment slot="title">Brewing Constellations: <em>how brewers really differ</em></Fragment>
  <MethodConstellations client:load />
  <noscript><p class="bp-noscript">The interactive sky needs JavaScript. Every brewer is compared in the table below.</p></noscript>

  <Fragment slot="body">
    <h2>Four separate axes</h2>
    <p>Brewers are often sorted into pour-over, immersion and pressure. That mixes up different things: espresso is percolation under pressure, and an AeroPress steeps like a press and is then pushed through paper by hand. Each axis here answers one question.</p>
    <h3>Contact: how water meets the coffee</h3>
    <ul>{order.map((k) => <li><strong>{CONTACT[k].label}.</strong> {CONTACT[k].line}</li>)}</ul>
    <h3>Filter: what holds the grounds back</h3>
    <p>Paper traps most of the coffee's oils and fine particles, so the cup is clearer and lighter-bodied; metal lets them through for more body; cloth sits between. Turkish coffee isn't filtered at all.</p>
    <ul>{Object.values(FILTER).sort((a, b) => a.order - b.order).map((f) => <li><strong>{f.label}.</strong> {f.line}</li>)}</ul>
    <h3>Force: what moves the water</h3>
    <ul>{Object.values(FORCE).sort((a, b) => a.order - b.order).map((f) => <li><strong>{f.label}.</strong> {f.line}</li>)}</ul>
    <p class="bp-note">A moka pot works at about 1.5 bar, nowhere near espresso's 9, which is why it makes strong coffee rather than espresso (Hoffmann). Espresso machines are usually set to about 9 bar; Rao notes flow peaks around 7–9 bar at the group head.</p>
    <h3>Time: how long water and coffee are in contact</h3>
    <p>From under half a minute for espresso to most of a day for cold brew. Finer grinds suit short contact and coarser grinds long contact, which is why each brewer has its own grind.</p>

    <h2>Every brewer compared</h2>
    <div class="mtab-wrap">
      <table class="mtab">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Brewer</th><th scope="col">Contact</th><th scope="col">Filter</th><th scope="col">Force</th><th scope="col">Time</th><th scope="col">Ratio</th><th scope="col">Recipe</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {rows.map((m) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">{m.label}</th>
              <td>{CONTACT[m.contact].label}</td>
              <td>{FILTER[m.filter].label}</td>
              <td>{FORCE[m.force].label}</td>
              <td class="mono">{timeText(m)}</td>
              <td class="mono">{ratioText(m)}</td>
              <td>{brewGuideHref(m) ? <a href={brewGuideHref(m)!}>Brew Guide</a> : <a href={`/blog/${m.guide.slug}/`}>Guide</a>}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="bp-note">Ratios are water to coffee by weight; espresso's is drink out to coffee in. Where the Brew Guide covers a brewer, these numbers are the Brew Guide's own. The phin, Turkish coffee, Clever Dripper and siphon use the recipes in our guides to those brewers.</p>

    <h2>Guides to each brewer</h2>
    <ul>
      {[...new Map(ATLAS.map((m) => [m.guide.slug, m])).values()].map((m) => <li><a href={`/blog/${m.guide.slug}/`}>{m.guide.title}</a></li>)}
    </ul>
    <p>Not sure what grind each one needs? The <a href="/tools/grind-guide/">Grind Guide</a> shows it, and the <a href="/tools/brew-ratio/">Brew Guide</a> builds the recipe for your cup.</p>

    <h2>Sources</h2>
    <ul class="bp-sources">
      {cited.map((s) => <li>{s.author}, <cite>{s.title}</cite>{s.year ? ` (${s.year})` : ''}{s.where ? `: ${s.where}` : ''}.</li>)}
    </ul>
  </Fragment>
</BenchPage>

<style>
  .mtab-wrap { overflow-x: auto; border: 1px solid #d9cdbd; border-radius: 12px; background: #fbf8f3; }
  .mtab { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 14.5px; }
  .mtab th, .mtab td { text-align: left; padding: 9px 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid #e6dccd; white-space: nowrap; }
  .mtab thead th { font: 500 11px/1 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #75655a; }
  .mtab tbody th { font-weight: 600; }
  .mtab .mono { font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 13.5px; }
  .mtab tr:last-child th, .mtab tr:last-child td { border-bottom: 0; }
</style>
